  "id": "free-play",
  "term": "free play",
  "definition": "Free play is a play context in early childhood that sits on a play continuum and differs from guided or teacher-directed play in how control is distributed between adults and children. In the source, it is marked by low-level reciprocal teacher-child interaction, with talk tending to stay at less inferential levels.",
